A cold nose wakes me.
I open my eyes and see Ludwig by the bed.
He is very hungry and wants breakfast.
I get up and go out into the kitchen.
He runs happily after me.
I find the bag of dog food.
Ludwig immediately jumps up against me.
"No, stop," I say firmly to him.
"You must not jump."
"Sit," I say and point at the floor.
He sits down and looks at me.
I pour the food into his bowl.
He wants to eat it immediately.
"Wait," I say quickly to him.
"You must wait nicely."
I place the bowl on the floor in front of him.
He sits completely still, and I pet him on the head.
"Go ahead, just eat it," I say with a smile.
